  "proof": "For T=(Y_A Z_B)K, T H T^-1=-H for real Xi and bipartite edgeZZ. Antiunitarity also flips i, hence T commutes with every generated evolution U. But |<ua|T u0>| is 0 or1, whereas |<Da|T D0>|=1/sqrt(C(n,a)); a is smaller color size. Required two columns contradict overlap preservation, even with independent phases. V leaves these low columns unchanged.",
  "scope": "Odd n; connected bipartite graph; no extra ancillas; exact low columns including r=0,a. No no-go claim for general native decoders.",
  "enlarged_algebra_scope": "Closure under adjoints of original Pauli generators spans the generated Lie algebra by Jacobi. Dimensions reaching 2^(2n-1)-2 certify continuous-control algebra su(2^(n-1)) plus su(2^(n-1)), excluding central globalX and identity. They provide no finite CZ-depth or fixed-layer ansatz guarantee.",
  "generic_rotation_primitives": {
    "ZZ": "H(target), CZ, Rx(target,theta), CZ, H(target)",
    "XX": "H(control), CZ, Rx(target,theta), CZ, H(control)",
    "CZ_per_rotation": 2,
    "single_qubit_gates_per_rotation": 3,
    "serial_native_moments": 5,
    "scope": "Exact conjugation constructions for exp(-i theta PP/2), adjacent pair; special angles can simplify. Counts are explicit upper bounds, not lower bounds."
  },
  "cost_caveat": "Controlled-reversal counts are explicit decomposition upper bounds, not lower bounds. SWAP/restore routes each CNOT separately. Arbitrary ZZ/XX rotations generally require2CZ; special Clifford angles may be cheaper. Routing, cancellation and finite depth remain unoptimized.",
  "odd_scope": "Even n has a self-complementary middle-count complication; paired-column construction is not asserted there.",
  "literature": [
    {
      "title": "Dicke-state preparation through global transverse control of Ising-coupled qubits",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12483",
      "finding": "Global control with all-to-all Ising interactions prepares specified symmetric states from a symmetric initial state; this is not a coherent unary decoder."
    },
    {
      "title": "Global variational quantum circuits for arbitrary symmetric state preparation",
      "url": "https://journals.aps.org/prresearch/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.7.L022072",
      "finding": "Uses global one-axis twisting and global rotations. Reported pulse steps and approximate fidelities are not native Willow CZ depths or simultaneous-column guarantees."
    },
    {
      "title": "The computational power of matchgates and the XY interaction on arbitrary graphs",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.1463",
      "finding": "General matchgates are classically simulable on paths/cycles and computationally universal on other connected graphs. This does not imply finite-size reachability for a fixed gate subset or this isometry."
    }
  ],
  "permutation_obstruction": "If U commutes with every qubit permutation and U|x>=|D_r>, then U P|x>=P|D_r>=|D_r>=U|x>, so P|x>=|x>. Thus such U cannot turn a nonsymmetric unary basis state into a symmetric Dicke state."
